Spec: Shell

Purpose:
  App skeleton: routes with fade transitions, the onboarding gate, the three-tab shell,
    theme mode, the active-ride deep link and the notice after a ride is saved.

Owns:
  ./*.dart
  /test/shell

References:
  /docs/specs/history/08-navigation-shell.md

Must:
  Routes are `/splash`, `/init`, `/init/photo`, `/init/photo/activity`, `/` with the children `/timer`, `/ride`
    and `/follow`; every route fades in and out over `180` ms.
  While onboarding state is loading the app shows the splash; without finished onboarding it goes to `/init`.
  A pending ride deep link opens `/ride` once and is cleared.
  The shell shows Home, History and Settings in a swipeable page view with a Material 3 navigation bar
    driven by one tab list.
  The shell owns the greeting selector and re-rolls the greeting each time Home settles as the current tab.
  Tapping a ride on Home switches to History and scrolls to that ride.
  Theme mode follows the stored preference; `system`, `light` and `dark` map to @ThemeMode.
